# Server-side only — read by api/explore.ts and api/critique.ts. Never
# prefix with VITE_ or it will be bundled into client code and exposed in
# the browser.
#
# Option A (simplest): plain Gemini API key. Get a free one from
# https://aistudio.google.com/apikey. Used whenever GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI
# is not "true".
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Option B: Vertex AI + Application Default Credentials. Requires a GCP
# project with the Vertex AI API and billing enabled.
#   Local dev: run `gcloud auth application-default login` (installs gcloud
#   first if you don't have it: https://cloud.google.com/sdk/docs/install),
#   then set GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT below.
#   Production (Vercel): interactive login isn't possible for serverless
#   functions — create a service account with the "Vertex AI User" role,
#   download its JSON key, and paste the *entire file contents* as
#   GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON in your Vercel project's env vars.
# GOOGLE_GENAI_USE_VERTEXAI=true
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_LOCATION=us-central1
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON=
